  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nCurrent analysis shows a departing low moving out of northeast \nMT. Lingering energy behind this system is expected to bring \nscattered rain/snow showers to areas of Billings through Sheridan,\nWY west through the day. With a small amount of instability \n(MUCAPE up to 200 J/kg), a few isolated thunderstorms cannot be \nruled out. Accumulations are likely to be low outside of higher \nterrain, unless under a thunderstorm. Additionally with the \ndeparting low, breezy winds 30-40 mph are expected across \nsoutheast MT through today. Ridging over the region will bring in \nwarm and dry conditions for the weekend and first half of next \nweek. A weak backdoor front may barely clip far east MT, slightly \nlimiting temperatures Monday, but no precip is expected with that.\nHigh temperatures over the weekend will warm from the 50s/60s to \nthe 60s/70s. Temperatures through Wednesday are then expected to \nbe in the 70s to low 80s across the region. Ensembles then look to\nbring in unsettled and potentially wet weather. There is still \nsome uncertainty on just where the low would set up with a better \nset up being to just to the south into WY. Watch the forecast as\nit will evolve. TS",
